          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-base text-ink/70 font-light leading-relaxed">
            <span class="mt-2 w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-purplePrimary opacity-60 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            {item}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">Online lessons may be the better place to start if:</p>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 pl-5 list-none">
        {[
          "Travel would make weekly lessons hard to keep up",
          "You're comfortable following verbal cues and checking your own setup",
          "You have a quiet space where you can stand and play with room to move",
          "The teacher you most want to learn from isn't nearby",
        ].map(item => (
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-base text-ink/70 font-light leading-relaxed">
            <span class="mt-2 w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-purplePrimary opacity-60 shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            {item}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">If you see yourself in both lists, that's common. In that case, the teacher matters more than the format. Someone who observes carefully, explains things more than one way, and adjusts to you will make either format work better.</p>

      <!-- Mid-article CTA -->
      <div class="mt-10 flex">
        <a href="/about" class="btn-secondary" aria-label="Learn about Rae's teaching approach at Vibrations Violin Studio">
          Learn About Rae's Teaching Approach
        </a>
