      <!-- Section 6 -->
      <h2 class="mt-12 font-heading font-bold text-ink" style="font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 1.75rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.025em;">Can You Change Formats Later?</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">The choice you make at the beginning doesn't have to be the one you keep. A student who starts in person to get their setup comfortable may later find online lessons easier to fit into a busy season. Someone who starts online may decide they'd like in-person time when they're refining tone or working through a stubborn habit.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">What helps most is being honest with your teacher about what's working and what isn't. Lessons should change as your needs change, and the format is one of the things you can talk through together.</p>

      <!-- FAQ -->
      <h2 class="mt-12 font-heading font-bold text-ink" style="font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 1.75rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.025em;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <h3 class="mt-8 font-heading font-semibold text-ink" style="font-size: 1.1rem; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Do online violin lessons cost less than in-person lessons?</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">Not necessarily. Many teachers price online and in-person lessons similarly, because you're still receiving individual instruction and feedback. The savings online are usually in travel time rather than the lesson fee, so it's worth asking each teacher directly.</p>

      <h3 class="mt-8 font-heading font-semibold text-ink" style="font-size: 1.1rem; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Is the first violin lesson different online?</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">A little. Part of a first online lesson goes to positioning the camera so the teacher can see your posture, bow arm, and left hand clearly. After that, the priorities are the same as in person: a comfortable setup, healthy habits, and a confident start.</p>

      <h3 class="mt-8 font-heading font-semibold text-ink" style="font-size: 1.1rem; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Can a young child take violin lessons online?</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">Some can, especially with a parent or caregiver nearby to help with setup and practice routines. Very young beginners often need more physical guidance, so in-person lessons can be an easier place to start. It depends on the individual child.</p>

      <h3 class="mt-8 font-heading font-semibold text-ink" style="font-size: 1.1rem; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Can a teacher hear my tone accurately over video?</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">Mostly, yes. Pitch, rhythm, and the overall shape of your sound come through clearly. Video calls do soften some of the finer details of tone, which is one reason in-person time can be especially useful when you're refining your sound.</p>

      <!-- Local SEO closing section -->
      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-lavender-200">
        <h2 class="font-heading font-bold text-ink" style="font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 1.75rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.025em;">Violin Lessons in Denver and Online</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">Vibrations Violin Studio offers private violin lessons for adults and children in Denver, Colorado, with online lessons available for students where that's a good fit. In either format, lessons are built around each student's goals, pacing, and questions.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">If you're not sure which format suits you or your child, you're welcome to reach out for a low-pressure conversation. We can talk through your goals, your schedule, and what kind of support would help most, then figure out a good place to start.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary inline-block mt-8" aria-label="Book a 15-minute intro call about online or in-person violin lessons">
          Book a 15-Minute Intro Call
